  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 249 AM EST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nToday-Fri...High pressure north of the area will continue an \nonshore (east) flow today that will gradually decrease through \nlate week as the ridge axis settles over the area. Rain chances \ndecrease to 20-30% today and then drier air will limit rain\nchances to10% or less Thu and Fri. Max temps will be above normal\nreaching the mid 80s. Heat indices will reach the upper 80s to\nnear 90 which will produce a minor HeatRisk for those sensitive to\nthe heat and without cooling or hydration. \n\nSat-Tue...A weak cool front is forecast push through the area \nSaturday but little moisture looks assocd with the boundary so\nkeeping rain chances out of the forecast. High pressure will build\nover the area behind the front Sun keeping conditions dry. Models\nare in disagreement about early next week with the GFS more\naggressive showing a deep cut-off low across the deep South\ngenerating a sfc low lifting NE out of the Gulf and a cold front\nsweeping across central FL Tue. The ECMWF is slower and weaker\nwith these features keeping conds dry through Tue then showing\nincreased rain chances mid week. For now, PoPs are limited to\n15-20% Mon-Tue. Highs in the low to mid 80s on Saturday fall to \nthe mid 70s to near 80 degrees Mon-Tue. Lows in the upper 50s \npossible mainly near to NW of I-4 early next week.",
